---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../../components/Footer.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
---

<Layout title="Concrete Calculators — Calculator Street" description="Concrete calculators for slabs, driveways & patios. Estimate cubic yards, bags & ready-mix cost with waste. US units, 2026 prices.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="mx-auto max-w-[1400px] px-6 py-6 max-md:px-4">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Construction", href: "/construction/" }, { label: "Concrete Calculators" }]} />
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[900px] pt-4">
      <h1 class="text-display-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-ink">Concrete Calculators</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Slabs, driveways and patios — yards, bags & ready-mix cost with waste. All tools handle feet, inches, yards and meters and show US short tons.</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2" role="list">
        <li><a href="/concrete-slab-calculator/" class="flex h-full flex-col rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas p-5 shadow-card hover:shadow-card-hover dark:bg-canvas"><h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Concrete Slab Calculator</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-5 text-body">Sq ft, yd³ & bags (40/60/80 lb) with waste & cost.</p><span class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-ink">Open →</span></a></li>
      </ul>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8">
        <section class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:bg-canvas">
          <h2 class="text-display-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">Which slab thickness?</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Patios and shed pads: 3.5–4 inches (4,000 psi). Driveways and garage floors: 5–6 inches. Sidewalks: 4 inches. Thicker adds volume fast — a 6-inch slab uses 50% more concrete than 4-inch over the same footprint. Confirm with local code and an engineer for loads. A 10×10 ft patio at 4 inches is 1.23 yd³ before waste; at 6 inches it’s 1.85 yd³.</p>
          <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md border border-hairline"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-canvas-soft font-mono text-[11px] text-mute"><tr><th class="px-3 py-2">USE</th><th class="px-3 py-2">THICKNESS</th><th class="px-3 py-2">YD³ FOR 10×10</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline"><tr><td class="px-3 py-2">Patio</td><td class="px-3 py-2">4 in</td><td class="px-3 py-2">1.23</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-2">Driveway</td><td class="px-3 py-2">6 in</td><td class="px-3 py-2">1.85</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-2">Shed pad</td><td class="px-3 py-2">3.5 in</td><td class="px-3 py-2">1.08</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
        </section>
        <section class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:bg-canvas">
          <h2 class="text-display-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">Ready-mix vs bags</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Under ~0.75 yd³ (30–40 bags of 80-lb) bags can be practical. Over 1–1.5 yd³ ready-mix is cheaper and faster — a 12×10 ft patio at 4 inches needs 74 bags of 80-lb with waste vs 1.63 yd³ ready-mix. Our slab calculator shows both so you can compare instantly: bags = ceil(cubic feet ÷ 0.60) for 80-lb.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Need base gravel? Size it with the <a href="/gravel-calculator/" class="text-link underline">Gravel Calculator</a>. For pavers instead of poured, see the <a href="/paver-calculator/" class="text-link underline">Paver Calculator</a>.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:bg-canvas">
          <h2 class="text-display-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">Sources & review</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Coverage: 80-lb = 0.60 ft³, 60-lb = 0.45 ft³, 40-lb = 0.30 ft³ per manufacturer yield. Reviewed by Vipul Otari, updated Aug 2026. Always verify with your supplier’s bag yield and engineer.</p>
        </section>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:bg-canvas"><h2 class="text-display-sm font-semibold text-ink">Planned</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Driveway concrete, footing, steps, bag & cost pages. Expanding as Search Console shows demand.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
